    "background_story": "Dutton was a renowned storm chaser who had spent his entire career studying the most extreme weather phenomena. Growing up in the Midwest, he had witnessed firsthand the devastating effects of tornadoes and was driven to understand their power. As a leading researcher, Dutton developed a state-of-the-art storm tracking system that allowed him to predict with uncanny accuracy when and where the most intense storms would strike. But it was his encounter with a massive EF5 tornado in Oklahoma that intensified his passion for his work. The experience left him shaken but more determined than ever to unravel the mysteries of these powerful storms. With renewed focus, Dutton's research took a dramatic leap forward, leading to breakthroughs in storm prediction and mitigation. His work has since saved countless lives and earned him international recognition.",
